TERMS
=====

This is a collection, not a work. Read this before redistributing anything
out of it.


THE SOFTWARE UNDER disk/
------------------------

Every program under `disk/` was written by somebody else, most of it
published between the mid-1980s and the mid-1990s. It was gathered from
places that have carried it in the open for decades: the OS-9 hobbyist
archives, the Hamburg OS-9 Users Group, EFFO user-group disks, usenet
postings from comp.sources.games and comp.sources.misc, and other public
preservation sites. It is collected here as a convenience -- one disk image
instead of a scatter of archives -- and for no other reason.

**Nothing here relicenses any of it.** Each program remains under whatever
copyright and terms its own author gave it, and those terms, not this file,
are what govern its use and redistribution. They vary widely:

- some is explicitly public domain
- some is under the GNU GPL, with the `COPYING` files kept in `disk/DOC/`
- some is freeware, distributable by the author's stated permission
- SB-Prolog is under SUNY Stony Brook's licence, which **requires** that the
  licence travel with the program (`disk/DOC/sbprolog/COPYING`)
- four EFFO programs carry their authors' request for no military use, and
  their `info_*` files ship beside them because that is what those terms ask
- some carries a copyright notice and no licence text at all -- larn, for
  instance, is "copyrighted 1986 by Noah Morgan" with no accompanying grant

`disk/SOURCES.txt` records what is known for each program, and says so
plainly where nothing is known rather than guessing. `disk/DOC/ORIGINS` names
the archive each one came out of. **If you intend to redistribute a program
from this collection, those files are your starting point, not this one.**

Assembling and indexing a collection is not authorship of the things
collected, and no claim is made over them here.

If you hold rights in something in this collection and would rather it were
not here, say so and it will be removed.


THE TOOLING
-----------

The part that was written for this repository -- `tools/`, `.github/`,
`README.md`, `notes/` -- is offered under the MIT licence, in
`tools/LICENSE`. It is a build script, an archive packer and two checkers.
They are kept deliberately separate from the above so that nothing about
them reads as a claim over the collection.


NO MICROWARE PRODUCT IS HERE
----------------------------

No Microware utilities, headers, libraries or `cio`. OS-9 is Microware's and
is still a current product; this collection is for people running it. The
programs were compiled with Microware's `cc`, which links its `cstart` and C
library -- that is what a compiler is for.
